senses.gloss:
अभि-काम, अस्, m. affection, desire; (अस्, आ, अम्),
affectionate, loving, desirous, with obj. in acc. or gen.;
(अम्), ind. with desire.

अभिगै अभि-गै, cl. 1. P. -गायति, -गातुम्,
to call to, to sing to; to fill with song; to enchant;
to sing, celebrate in song.

अभिचुद् अभि-चुद्, Caus. P. -चोदयति, -यि-
तुम्, to impel, drive; to inflame, animate, embolden;
to invite; to fix, settle; to announce, inquire for.

अभि-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, produced all around; born
in consequence of; born, produced; noble, well-born;
obtained by birth, inbred; fit, proper; wise, learned;
handsome; (अम्), n. nativity.
—अभिजात-ता, f. high
birth, nobility.

अभि-निविष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, well versed or profi-
cient in, conversant or familiar with; intent on;
attentive, engrossed; endowed with; determined;
(अम्), n. persevering.
—अभिनिविष्ट-ता, f. state of
being so.

अभि-नीत, अस् आ, अम्, brought near, adduced;
performed; highly finished or ornamented; fit, pro-
per; friendly, kind, patient; impatient, passionate (?).

अभीपत् अभीपत्, m. (fr. अभि and अप्;
cf. अनूप), Ved. a pond or any spot in which water
collects; favour (?).

अभिपू अभि-पू, cl. 1. A., Ved. -पवते,
-वितुम्, to be cleared, to flow purified towards or for;
to blow against; to make bright, glorify.

अभिप्रतिगॄ अभि-प्रति-गॄ, cl. 9. P. A.
-गृणाति, -णीते, -गरितुम् or -रीतुम्, to call out to;
to welcome; to answer in singing; to assent.

अभि-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, going near, approaching;
aiming at; (अस्), m. aim, purpose, intention, with,
desire; goal; meaning, sense, reference.

अभिमेथिका अभि-मेथिका, f. (rt. मेथ्),
Ved. insulting or injurious speech; obscene expression;
imprecation.

अभि-योक्तव्य or अभि-योज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be
reproved or rebuked; to be prosecuted, indictable;
assailable.

अभिरूप अभि-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, corresponding
with; conformable to, congruous; in accordance with;
pleasing, handsome, desirable, well formed, beautiful;
wise, learned; (अस्), m. the moon; Śiva; Viṣṇu;
Kāmadeva.
—अभिरूप-पति, इस्, m. having an agree-
able master (a rite) to secure such a master in the
next world.

अभि-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, m.f. (from श्री connected with श्रि),
Ved. joining, connecting one's self with, mixing;
combining, holding together, arranging, putting in
order, united, approaching; having recourse to,
worthy to be had recourse to; respected; shining;
powerful.

अभिषाच् अभि-षाच्, क्, क्, क् (rt. सच्), Ved.
following; honouring, paying attention to, devoted;
defeating.

अभिसंस्कृ अभि-संस्-कृ (-सम्-कृ), cl. 8. P.
-करोति, -कर्तुम्, to shape, form; to make, render;
to consecrate.

अभिसन्धा 1. अभि-सन्-धा (-सम्-धा), cl.
3. P. -दधाति, -धातुम्, to aim at; overcome;
deceive; calumniate; declare; add; prefer.

अभि-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck; beaten; smitten;
killed; humbled, subdued, broken down; obstructed;
multiplied.

अभीरु अ-भीरु, उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ, unterrific;
fearless, undaunted; (उस्), m., N. of Bhairava or Śiva;
(उस् or ऊस्), f., N. of a plant, Asparagus Racemosus.
—अभीरु-पत्त्री, f. a plant, the leaves of which are
like those of the plant Abhiru (see above); the plant
Abhīru.

आभिजात्य, अम्, n. (fr. अभि-जात, rt. जन्), the
nature or state of a man of noble birth, nobility;
birth, family, rank, learning.

आभिषेचनिक आभिषेचनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.
अभि-षेचन), relating to the inauguration of a king;
serving for it.
